@lang en
IMPORT `ocar-tests-fixtures`

-- EVIDENCE FOR THE FINDINGS in NOTES.md, section 4. Each assertion states what the instrument,
-- as encoded, answers in a case where the answer is surprising. They are true assertions: a
-- finding is a defect in the document, demonstrated, not a failing test. Where a finding can
-- only be read, NOTES.md says "reading only" and nothing is asserted here.

§ `Findings, demonstrated`

GIVEN p IS A `The policy`
      l IS A `The loss`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most payable on` p `for` l MEANS
    `the amount payable on the claim, with no reduction under Article 16` (`a claim on` p `for` l)

GIVEN p IS A `The policy`
      l IS A `The loss`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the least payable on` p `for` l MEANS
    `the amount payable on the claim, after the largest reduction Article 16 allows` (`a claim on` p `for` l)

GIVEN cd IS A `The conduct after the loss`
      ls IS A `The load and speed`
GIVETH A `The loss`
`a collision repaired for 10,000,000, conduct` cd `, load` ls MEANS
    `a loss on` (YMD 2026 6 10) `by` `collision or impact, including with another object` `, circumstances` (`the circumstances with` EMPTY) `, load` ls `, conduct` cd `, items` (LIST `a part repaired for` 10_000_000)

§§ `X1 — exercising a data right ends the cover, at a 30% loss, or with nothing back`

-- Personal data clause 10 (src:1242-1249) with 3.2.2 (src:184-190): an Insured who exercises a
-- right under clause 5 of Article 9 of Decree 13/2023 on 1 July ends the contract as if the
-- Policyholder had terminated it: 70% of the unexpired premium; nothing if a loss happened.
#ASSERT `data clause 10 — the contract ends, on` `the plain policy` `, when a right is exercised under clause` 5
#ASSERT `data clause 10 — the refund, on` `the plain policy` `, a right exercised under clause` 5 `on` (YMD 2026 7 1) `,` FALSE `,` 0 EQUALS JUST ((70% TIMES 12_000_000 TIMES 183) DIVIDED BY 365)
#ASSERT `data clause 10 — the refund, on` `the plain policy` `, a right exercised under clause` 5 `on` (YMD 2026 7 1) `,` TRUE `,` 0 EQUALS JUST 0

§§ `X2 — the battery under BS01: relieved by (c) and BS01, depreciated "in every case" by (d)`

-- 14.1.2(c) src:823-827 and BS01 src:1017-1023 do not except a battery from "no depreciation";
-- 14.1.2(d) src:828-833 depreciates it in every case. The encoding takes (d) (fork F29): 50%.
`the 2022 contract with BS01 on the 2022 car` MEANS `the 2026 policy with` (LIST `clause accepted and paid in full and on time:` `BS01 no depreciation on new parts and materials`)
#ASSERT NOT `BS01 — the clause leaves this kind of part to depreciation` `a battery`
#ASSERT NOT `14.1.2(c) — the no-depreciation clause leaves this kind of part to depreciation` `a battery`
#ASSERT `14.1 — the cost allowed, on` `the 2022 contract with BS01 on the 2022 car` `for` `the plain collision` `, for the item` (`a` `a battery` `replaced new for` 10_000_000) EQUALS 5_000_000

§§ `X3 — notice in time under 5.2 is late under 16.1.1`

-- A loss on Wednesday 10 June, notified on Wednesday 17 June: within 5 WORKING days (5.2,
-- src:330-332), but not within 5 DAYS (16.1.1, src:917-920): the Insurer may cut 5% to 10%.
`a collision notified on 17 June` MEANS `a collision repaired for 10,000,000, conduct` (`the conduct, notified on` (JUST (YMD 2026 6 17)) `, premium that should have been paid` 12_000_000 `, where` EMPTY) `, load` `normal load`
#ASSERT `5.2 — the loss was notified in time: lost on` (YMD 2026 6 10) `, notified on` (YMD 2026 6 17) `, skipping` `the test calendar`
#ASSERT `16.1.1 — notice of the loss was not sent within 5 days, for` `a collision notified on 17 June`
#ASSERT `the least payable on` `the plain policy` `for` `a collision notified on 17 June` EQUALS 8_550_000

§§ `X4 — one more passenger, a child, and the reduction disappears`

-- 12.18 (src:683-688) does not count children under 7; 16.1.5 (src:962-964) does. In a 5-seat
-- car, 7 adults: 40% over by both counts; no exclusion (under 50%), a 40% reduction. Add one child
-- under 7: 12.18 still counts 7 (40%: no exclusion), 16.1.5 counts 8 (60%: not "under 50%", so
-- no reduction). The more overloaded car is paid in full.
`a collision with 7 adults` MEANS `a collision repaired for 10,000,000, conduct` `good conduct` `, load` (`carrying` 0 `, persons counting children` 7 `, not counting them` 7 `, speed over the limit` NOTHING)
`a collision with 7 adults and a child` MEANS `a collision repaired for 10,000,000, conduct` `good conduct` `, load` (`carrying` 0 `, persons counting children` 8 `, not counting them` 7 `, speed over the limit` NOTHING)
#ASSERT `the least payable on` `the plain policy` `for` `a collision with 7 adults` EQUALS 5_700_000
#ASSERT `the least payable on` `the plain policy` `for` `a collision with 7 adults and a child` EQUALS 9_500_000

§§ `X5 — termination: five working days' notice, or on receipt?`

-- 3.2.1 (src:179-183): notice at least 5 working days before; 3.2.2 (src:190-192): the contract
-- ends when the Insurer receives the notice.
#ASSERT `3.2.1 — the earliest date a termination noticed on` (YMD 2026 10 5) `may take effect, skipping` `the test calendar` EQUALS YMD 2026 10 12
#ASSERT `3.2.2 — the date the contract ends on the Policyholder's notice received on` (YMD 2026 10 5) EQUALS YMD 2026 10 5

§§ `X6 — untruthful claim documents: all, or at most 30%`

-- 12.22 (src:698-701): excluded if the Insurer PROVES the information untruthful. 16.1.4 (src:950-
-- 951): reduced by up to 30% where the Owner was untruthful, no proof required.
#ASSERT `the most payable on` `the plain policy` `for` (`a collision with` (`the circumstances with` (LIST `fact 12.22 proven untruthful`)) `, items` (LIST `a part repaired for` 10_000_000)) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the least payable on` `the plain policy` `for` (`a collision repaired for 10,000,000, conduct` (`the conduct where` (LIST `conduct untruthful`)) `, load` `normal load`) EQUALS 6_650_000

§§ `X7 — BS04 beyond its sub-limit`

-- BS04 (src:1067-1076) cancels 14.1.2(a) and says nothing of a loss beyond the sub-limit.
`90,000,000 already paid under BS04` MEANS `The earlier claims in the period` WITH
    `indemnity already paid under BS04 in the period`    IS 90_000_000
    `parts losses already paid under BS05 in the period` IS 0
#ASSERT REFUSED `the amount payable on the claim, with no reduction under Article 16` (`a claim on` (`the under-insured policy with` (LIST `BS04 with a sub-limit of` 100_000_000)) `for` (`a collision with` (`the circumstances with` EMPTY) `, items` (LIST `a part repaired for` 20_000_000)) `, earlier` `90,000,000 already paid under BS04` `, journey` `no journey costs`) BECAUSE "BS04 does not say how a partial loss is settled beyond the sub-limit"

§§ `X8 — BS05 on a contract under 12 months`

#ASSERT REFUSED `BS05 — the number of parts losses covered on` (`a policy from` (YMD 2026 1 1) `to` (YMD 2026 6 30) `, with` (LIST `clause accepted and paid in full and on time:` `BS05 loss of parts`)) BECAUSE "BS05 states no limit for a contract shorter than 12 months"

§§ `X9 — BS03's electrical cover and 12.13's "whatever the cause"`

-- Without BS03, a natural-catastrophe flood that shorts the electrics is excluded by 12.13's
-- second limb (src:653-656), though the flood is an insured peril (src:569-570).
`flood-shorted electrics` MEANS `a` `an ordinary part` `repaired for` 8_000_000 `where` (LIST `item short circuit`)
#ASSERT `12 — the exclusions of the item, on` `the plain policy` `for` (`a loss by` `a natural catastrophe` `, items` (LIST `flood-shorted electrics`)) `:` `flood-shorted electrics` EQUALS LIST `12.13 electrical or mechanical breakdown`
-- With BS03, on the flood-water peril, the encoding lets BS03 prevail (fork F21).
#ASSERT `12 — the exclusions of the item, on` (`the 2026 policy with` (LIST `clause accepted and paid in full and on time:` `BS03 flood damage`)) `for` (`a loss by` `driving into flood water` `, items` (LIST `flood-shorted electrics`)) `:` `flood-shorted electrics` EQUALS EMPTY

§§ `X10 — no value for a vehicle imported new`

#ASSERT REFUSED `13 — the value of the vehicle when insured, on` (`a policy with no market value on` (`a car` `imported new` `, new:` FALSE `, first registered` (YMD 2022 3 15) `, made in` 2022 `, used as` `none of the uses listed in 14.1.2(b)`) `, customs rate` NOTHING) BECAUSE "13.2 gives no value for a new vehicle, or one imported new, whose market value cannot be determined"

§§ `X14 — the Insurer's discretion under Article 16`

-- Repairing without approval (16.1.3, src:936-940): the same claim may be paid 9,500,000 or
-- 1,900,000, at the Insurer's choice of any rate up to 80%.
`a collision repaired without approval` MEANS `a collision repaired for 10,000,000, conduct` (`the conduct where` (LIST `conduct dismantled without approval`)) `, load` `normal load`
#ASSERT `the most payable on` `the plain policy` `for` `a collision repaired without approval` EQUALS 9_500_000
#ASSERT `the least payable on` `the plain policy` `for` `a collision repaired without approval` EQUALS 1_900_000

§§ `X16 — the 16.1 chapeau's incomplete comparative`

#ASSERT REFUSED `the amount payable on the claim, after the largest reduction Article 16 allows` (`a claim on` (`the plain policy with deductible` NOTHING `, reduction level` (JUST (10%)) `, premium paid` 12_000_000 `, owing allowed` FALSE `, other policies` EMPTY) `for` `the plain collision`) BECAUSE "16.1 lets the contract state a reduction level, but its comparative is incomplete"

§§ `X20 — the payment period that never starts`

-- 4.2 (src:243-245): where the Insurer cannot itself verify the file, the file is complete only on
-- the authority's conclusion; with none, the 15-working-day period has no start.
#ASSERT `4.2 — the date the file counts as complete` FALSE (YMD 2026 6 10) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `X21 — a lower risk, a refused reduction, and a 30% exit`

-- Article 6 (src:376-385): the risk falls, the Insurer refuses to cut the premium; the only exit is
-- 3.2.2: 70% of the unexpired premium (here from 1 July), or nothing after an insured event.
#ASSERT `6 — the Policyholder may terminate under 3.2.2` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `3.2.2 — the refund on the Policyholder's termination` `the plain policy` `on` (YMD 2026 7 1) `,` FALSE `,` 0 EQUALS (70% TIMES 12_000_000 TIMES 183) DIVIDED BY 365

§§ `X22 — double insurance that the Law would not call double, stacked on under-insurance`

-- Article 9 (src:503-523) shares a loss between insurers whatever the total sum insured; the Law
-- (Article 49(1), law text lines 964-968) calls it double insurance only where the total exceeds
-- the value. Two policies of 300,000,000 each on a 600,000,000 car: the total is the value. OPES
-- is also insured below value, so 14.1.2(a) halves the loss and Article 9 halves it again
-- (fork F4): of a 10,000,000 loss, 2,500,000, less the deductible.
`another insurer's policy of 300,000,000` MEANS `Another policy on the vehicle` WITH
    `issued by another insurer`                            IS TRUE
    `sum insured`                                          IS 300_000_000
    `same subject, same conditions and same insured event` IS TRUE
    `in force at the time of the loss`                     IS TRUE
`OPES's half of the cover` MEANS `The policy` WITH
    `vehicle`                                                         IS `the private car`
    `date the contract was concluded`                                 IS YMD 2026 1 1
    `start of the insurance period`                                   IS YMD 2026 1 1
    `last day of the insurance period`                                IS YMD 2026 12 31
    `sum insured`                                                     IS 300_000_000
    `market value when insured`                                       IS JUST 600_000_000
    `price of the vehicle new (100%)`                                 IS 800_000_000
    `minimum remaining-quality rate in the import customs declaration` IS NOTHING
    `deductible stated in the contract`                               IS NOTHING
    `reduction level stated in the contract`                          IS NOTHING
    `premium`                                                         IS 6_000_000
    `premium paid`                                                    IS 6_000_000
    `last day for paying the premium`                                 IS YMD 2026 1 15
    `the Insurer agreed that the premium may be owed`                 IS FALSE
    `supplementary clauses`                                           IS EMPTY
    `other policies on the vehicle`                                   IS LIST `another insurer's policy of 300,000,000`
    `the personal data clause is part of the contract`                IS TRUE
    `the data subject agreed to the whole personal data clause`       IS TRUE
#ASSERT `the most payable on` `OPES's half of the cover` `for` `the plain collision` EQUALS 2_000_000

§§ `X23 — one dong moves the whole cost of the assessment`

#ASSERT `7 — the party who pays for the independent assessment and the court fees` "collision" 10_000_000 "collision" 10_000_000 EQUALS `the Policyholder`
#ASSERT `7 — the party who pays for the independent assessment and the court fees` "collision" 10_000_000 "collision" 10_000_001 EQUALS `the Insurer`

§§ `X25 — any insured event forfeits the refund, even one that paid nothing`

-- A scrape repaired for 400,000 is below the 500,000 deductible: 12.20 pays nothing. It is still
-- an insured event (fork F6), so the Policyholder who then terminates on 1 July gets nothing back
-- under 3.2.2 (src:188-190), where without it 4,210,849.31... would be refunded.
#ASSERT `the most payable on` `the plain policy` `for` (`a collision with` (`the circumstances with` EMPTY) `, items` (LIST `a part repaired for` 400_000)) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `3.2.2 — the refund on the Policyholder's termination` `the plain policy` `on` (YMD 2026 7 1) `,` TRUE `,` 0 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `3.2.2 — the refund on the Policyholder's termination` `the plain policy` `on` (YMD 2026 7 1) `,` FALSE `,` 0 EQUALS (70% TIMES 12_000_000 TIMES 183) DIVIDED BY 365
